
# =====================================================
# HEYBIO ↗ — LOCAL ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION TEMPLATE
# Your world. One link.
# A product of DIPO LABS
# =====================================================
#
# PURPOSE:
# This file documents the local development bindings.
#
# IMPORTANT:
# - Never put actual private secrets in this file.
# - Copy the required values into .dev.vars.
# - Cloudflare Workers uses .dev.vars locally.
# - Production bindings are configured separately.
# - Never commit .dev.vars.
#
# =====================================================
# 01 — SUPABASE AUTHENTICATION
# =====================================================

# Supabase Project Settings > Project URL
SUPABASE_URL="https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co"

# Supabase Project Settings > API Keys
# Use the public publishable key, not the secret key.
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="sb_publishable_REPLACE_ME"
# Supabase Project Settings > API Keys > Secret keys (default).
# SERVER ONLY. Never expose this in browser code or commit the real value.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY="sb_secret_REPLACE_ME"


# =====================================================
# 02 — CLOUDFLARE TURNSTILE
# =====================================================
#
# DEVELOPMENT ONLY:
# The following are official testing credentials.
# They do not provide real bot protection.
# NEVER use them on the production website.
#
# Production requires real site/secret keys and
# backend verification of each Turnstile token.

TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY="1x00000000000000000000AA"

TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY="1x0000000000000000000000000000000AA"


# =====================================================
# 03 — GOOGLE AUTHENTICATION
# =====================================================
#
# Google authentication is configured in:
#
# Supabase Dashboard
# > Authentication
# > Sign In / Providers
# > Google
#
# Do not add the Google OAuth Client Secret here.
#
# Verify the following externally:
#
# 1. Google provider enabled in Supabase.
# 2. Google Client ID and Secret configured there.
# 3. Google Cloud has Supabase OAuth callback URI.
# 4. Supabase redirect allowlist contains the
#    exact HEYBIO /auth/callback URL.
# 5. Test Google account is authorized if the
#    OAuth application is in Testing mode.
#
# No additional Google secret is required here
# for the current server-side OAuth implementation.


# =====================================================
# 04 — ADDITIONAL BACKEND SECRETS
# =====================================================
#
# Add only when the corresponding backend modules
# have been inspected and configured.
#
# Examples of future systems:
#
# - Server-side privileged Supabase operations
# - Razorpay subscriptions and verified webhooks
# - Payment reconciliation
# - Admin operations
# - Transactional email
#
# Do not invent environment variable names or
# enable unused credentials ahead of implementation.


# =====================================================
# 05 — PRODUCTION SECURITY RULES
# =====================================================
#
# - Use real Turnstile credentials on production.
# - Configure Cloudflare Worker secrets securely.
# - Keep database and payment secrets server-side.
# - Enable Row Level Security in Supabase.
# - Validate user access on the backend.
# - Never commit secrets into Git.
# - Never expose secrets through API responses.
#
# =====================================================
# END — HEYBIO ENVIRONMENT TEMPLATE
# =====================================================
